{
  "_note": "Adversarial benchmark for the build optimizer. Sixteen champions chosen to stress DIFFERENT parts of the scoring system rather than to be strong, each run under three scenarios. Expected properties are structural claims about what a correct answer looks like, not a copy of any particular build: a range, not a fingerprint. Where captured top-50 builds exist they are reported alongside as independent evidence, because a structural check can pass on a build no human would run. A FAIL is not automatically a bug: it says the build has a different shape from every captured build of that champion, which is worth looking at either way.",
  "_scenarios": {
    "A_pure": "The stated objective alone, ranked on the variant that expresses it.",
    "B_comp": "The same champion against a named enemy composition, scored as the champion's OBJECTIVE over an evaluation vector computed against that comp's damage split. It used to rank on score_vs_comp, which is 0.45*time-to-kill-their-carry + 0.55*durability and has no support term at all -- so an enchanter was ranked by a metric that cannot see her job.",
    "C_constrained": "Maximise the OBJECTIVE subject to surviving, as a hard filter rather than a penalty term. It used to maximise dps8 regardless of objective, which is the wrong thing to maximise for an enchanter outright."
  },
  "_itemClasses": {
    "damage": "carries any of ad, ap, crit, attackSpeed, physicalPen, magicPen, lethality",
    "defensive": "carries any of armor, mr, hp",
    "pureTank": "defensive stats and NO damage stat at all"
  },
  "survivalSeconds": {
    "_note": "Seconds alive under FOCUS_DPS (2200, roughly three attackers). Scenario C constrains on the champion's OWN minSurvivalSeconds rather than one global number: 8s is 17,600 effective health, which no build in the game reaches, so a single threshold made the constraint either vacuous or unsatisfiable.",
    "perChampion": true
  },
